# Stack Conventions

This is a Next.js 15 (App Router) + React 19 + TypeScript + Tailwind + Zustand project.

## Components
- Functional components only. Default to Server Components; add `"use client"` only when you need state, effects, or browser APIs.
- One component per file; name the file after the component (`Button.tsx`).
- Keep components small. Pull reusable logic into `hooks/` and pure helpers into `lib/`.

## State
- Local UI state: `useState`. Shared OS/app state: the Zustand store in `store/os-store.ts`.
- Don't add new global state unless two unrelated components truly need it.

## Styling
- Tailwind utility classes only; merge conditional classes with the `cn`/`clsx` helpers in `lib/utils.ts`.
- Reuse existing UI primitives in `components/ui/` before creating new ones.

## Data & types
- Static content lives in `data/`. Keep types close to where they're used; avoid premature shared type files.
- No `any`. Prefer precise types and let inference do the work.

## Before finishing
Run `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, and `npm run build`. All must pass.
